    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1622">

                <pb facs="1321" n="1205" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1205"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/133.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 204.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 3, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 194 of the
                    24th ultimo as to negotiations proceeding between Señor Carlos Constantino
                    Arosemena, Minister of Public Works, and Messrs. J. M. Hyatt and Robert Wilcox,
                    relative to the signature of the contract between the Panaman Government and
                    these gentlemen for the construction of a railway from Antón to Santiago, etc.,
                    I have the honor to inform you <pb facs="1322" n="1206" xml:id="pg1206"/> that
                    Señor Chiarí, Minister of Foreign Affairs, has now advised mo that the contract
                    will not be signed by this administration, which, owing to the fact that it is
                    so near its expiration, will not sign any more contracts, believing this to be
                    improper.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Percival Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
